# Defensive ignores for the curated experiments/ tree.
#
# The curated tree is built by selectively copying only small, high-signal
# artifacts (see README.md). These rules are a safety net so that re-running a
# build or dropping raw artifacts here can never accidentally commit the bulky
# per-case outputs, binary dumps, verbose logs, or secrets that live in the
# upstream un-curated result trees.

# --- Bulk per-case outputs (kept only as renamed exemplars under samples/) ---
results.jsonl
*.results.jsonl
metric_logs/
generated_best_outputs_valset/
instruction_proposer_inpouts.jsonl

# --- Heavy / binary artifacts ---
*.pkl
*.bin
run_log.txt
run_log_stderr.txt
*.stderr
round-*.json

# --- Secrets — never commit ---
.env
.envrc

# --- But DO keep the curated format exemplars under samples/ ---
!samples/
!samples/**
